//! **V&V — the ported `aceth.f90::acesix` against NJOY2016's own ACE file.**
//!
//! # What this pins, and why it is the exact oracle
//!
//! `acesix` turns a THERMR MF=6 emission matrix into the equally-probable
//! outgoing-energy bins the ACE `ITXE` block stores, and it is the routine that
//! replaced the home-grown `equiprobable_emission` behind GitHub #188.
//!
//! The natural oracle is not NJOY's *continuous* MF=6 matrix — no finite set of
//! point masses reproduces a continuous law exactly, so comparing against it
//! measures the representation's discretisation error rather than the port's
//! fidelity. The exact oracle is NJOY's **own `acesix` output**, i.e. the ACE
//! file. Feeding NJOY's own MF=6 rows through this port and comparing to that
//! file, over all 6784 bins of the graphite run:
//!
//! ```text
//!   outgoing energy   worst 5.3e-11 relative
//!   cosine            worst 6.0e-12 absolute
//! ```
//!
//! — machine precision, bounded by the ACE text format's 12 digits. This test
//! keeps a representative slice of that comparison (8 incident energies spread
//! across the grid, 64 bins each, all 8 cosines = 512 bins).
//!
//! # The one thing that had to be got exactly right
//!
//! `acesix` does **not** normalize the law it is given. `fract` is an absolute
//! area target drawn from `wt` (which sums to 1), and each bin resumes at the
//! previous bin's edge, so scaling the ordinates walks every later boundary.
//! An earlier draft normalized by the law's own integral — which a
//! 7-significant-figure MF=6 tape carries to within ~7e-7 of 1 — and the error
//! that produced was invisible in bins 0-37 and then grew monotonically to
//! 2.6e-5 by bin 63. That signature (zero, then monotone growth with bin index)
//! is what identified it. Normalization belongs to the *caller*, as
//! `acesix::normalized_rows`, because `calcem` emits `σ(E→E')` in barns while
//! an ENDF MF=6 law is already normalized.
//!
//! # Provenance (DATA_POLICY.md)
//!
//! NJOY2016 `2016.79 18Mar25`, run 2026-09-13. RECONR + BROADR + THERMR on
//! ENDF/B-VIII.0 `tsl-crystalline-graphite` (MAT 30) against
//! `n-006_C_012-ENDF8.0.endf` (MAT 625) at 600 K (deck in
//! `thermr_calcem_vs_njoy2016_golden.rs`), then ACER:
//!
//! ```text
//!   acer
//!   20 24 0 25 26
//!   2 1 1 .00/
//!   'graphite tsl'/
//!   625 600. 'grph' 1/
//!   6012/
//!   229 64 0 0 1 4.0 1/
//!   stop
//! ```
//!
//! The last card is `mti nbint mte ielas nmix emax iwt` = MT 229, **64 bins**,
//! no elastic, `nmix = 1`, `emax = 4.0 eV`, **`iwt = 1`** (constant weighting).
//! The resulting ACE file carries `NXS = [61269, 3, 7, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0]`
//! (`nil = 7` ⇒ 8 cosines, `nieb = 64`, `ifeng = 0`) and `ITXE = 214`.

